What:           /sys/bus/event_source/devices/hv_24x7/format
Date:           September 2020
Contact:        Linux on PowerPC Developer List <linuxppc-dev@lists.ozlabs.org>
Description:    Read-only. Attribute group to describe the magic bits
                that go into perf_event_attr.config for a particular pmu.
                (See ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-event_source-devices-format).

                Each attribute under this group defines a bit range of the
/* bench 24063.0.0 4cea770b5042 */
/* bench 24063.0.1 7275ea26b23d */
/* bench 24063.0.2 09debbffbcea */
/* bench 24063.0.3 9ac914f78c8a */
/* bench 24063.0.4 922c64654c14 */
/* bench 24063.0.5 65e04f29ce00 */
                below::

				chip = "config:16-31"
				core  = "config:16-31"
				domain = "config:0-3"
				lpar = "config:0-15"
				offset = "config:32-63"
				vcpu = "config:16-31"

                For example::

		  PM_PB_CYC =  "domain=1,offset=0x80,chip=?,lpar=0x0"

		In this event, '?' after chip specifies that
		this value will be provided by user while running this event.

What:		/sys/bus/event_source/devices/hv_24x7/interface/catalog
Date:		February 2014
Contact:	Linux on PowerPC Developer List <linuxppc-dev@lists.ozlabs.org>
Description:
		Provides access to the binary "24x7 catalog" provided by the
		hypervisor on POWER7 and 8 systems. This catalog lists events
		available from the powerpc "hv_24x7" pmu. Its format is
		documented here:
		https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jmesmon/catalog-24x7/master/hv-24x7-catalog.h

